		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-01T23:38:44Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1898,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Wind): Strip trailing slash from workspace folder URI parameter\n\nMountain's `BuildInitialUrl` sources the initial workspace from `~/.land/workspaces/RecentlyOpened.json`, which stores URIs with a trailing slash. After stripping the `file://` scheme and percent-encoding the path for the `?folder=` query parameter, the decoded value still ends in `/`. On macOS APFS, a workspace folder URI with a trailing slash prevents `IUriIdentityService.extUri.relativePath` and `ILabelService.getUriLabel` from computing relative paths, causing breadcrumbs to render absolute `/Volumes/...` paths instead of workspace-relative segments like `Source > Foo > Bar`.\n\nNormalize the decoded `folder` value by stripping trailing slashes (preserving a bare root `/`) before constructing the URI. Tighten the `Workspace` identifier guard to only build the object when a normalized folder parameter is present.",
			"SHA": "aa6aea4b1e3b66fda182deed1ec154c905c16d2d"
		},
